2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] It looks like “testing bumpmodel” isn’t a valid user‐level command in Slop Fountain’s CLI. The
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] token‐cost accounting logic (the `bumpModel` function) is invoked automatically internally after
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] each API call, so you won’t invoke it directly at the “/…” prompt.
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] 
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] If you really want to exercise it in isolation, you can call it in code—for example:
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] 
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] 
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] // assume you’ve imported bumpModel already:
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] import { bumpModel } from "./slopfountain.ts";
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] 
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] // fake API usage report:
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] const usage = { prompt_tokens: 10, completion_tokens: 5 };
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] const elapsedSeconds = 1.23;
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] const spentTokens: [number,number] = [10, 5];
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] const account = "openai";   // your provider key
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] 
2025-09-24 12:11:08 [codex-mini-latest] // this will update roha.mut[grokModel] and roha.lode[account].credit
